    "created_at": "2017-02-17T03:29:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-17T03:29:36Z",
    "body": "Strictly speaking this is already allowed, because the [preload attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#attr-media-preload) and no behavior is required. I don't think this is great, though, it means that almost no shared tests at all can be written for the attribute.\r\n\r\nFor a long time the behavior of Chrome for Android was to load nothing until the video began playing, so it's probably web compatible to not load anything until on-screen.\r\n\r\nIn an ideal balance between responsiveness and data savings, media would begin preloading just before a video becomes visible, so that it can be playing immediately. It's probably not write a heuristic that does this well, but with enough control sites might be able to do a good job themselves. Would that be worthwhile?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/280540234/reactions",
