    "created_at": "2017-02-17T09:45:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-17T09:45:53Z",
    "body": "I agree that changing preload to depend on visibility might not be a good idea because it could cause more harm than good. We are risking websites moving away from preload and doing their own loading where we would have no control as browsers. Instead, browsers can have special preload behaviours in some situations. For example, Chrome Android still do not preload media files for some low end devices or when Data Saver is on.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
