    "created_at": "2017-02-21T09:49:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-21T12:44:51Z",
    "body": "It's hard to estimate the preload usage as we don't have direct record of how much the attribute is used but only of the effective preload value. Though, for the record, only 4% of page loads have an HTMLMediaElement so all data about preload have to be looked within that context.\r\n\r\n@dalecurtis wouldn't requiring preloading to be visible actually make preload entirely moot? Let say I have a video in an article set as &lt;video autoplay muted>, does that mean it will start loading when visible then play later, potentially breaking the experience I was building for my users? (ie. get the animation to play while reading the article). Asking websites to switch to MSE for things like that sounds a bit too much IMO.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
